  "worked_solution": "The polar curve $r=3$ is a circle of radius $3$ centered at the origin. It crosses the positive $x$-axis at the point where $r=3$ and $\\theta =0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039331/assets/63d6e0d36e3d345561b1c4c20d7d19cb34ae6bd3b7543c042be288d8fcdb12e7.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(3,0).$",
